==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*arpa||barley}}. Probably borrowed into {{cog|xgn-pro|*arbaï}} and {{cog|mnc|ᠠᡵᡶᠠ}}, although some [[w:Altaic theory|Altaicists]] consider them related through common inheritance. Another less secure comparison is {{cog|ja|粟|tr=awa|t=[[foxtail millet]]}}.

The Turkic form is sometimes compared with {{cog|ira-pro|*arpasyaH|t=barley}} which is not found outside East Iranian. While Blažek (2012) prefers an [[Indo-European]] (Iranian) origin of the Altaic words for ‘barley’, Hyllestedt argues that several facts do point to a borrowing in the reverse direction. One possible Indo-European cognate for the Iranian word is {{cog|grc|ἄλφιτον||t=barley-groats}}, but the comparison is unsecure.

Cognate with {{cog|otk|tr=arpa}}, {{cog|cv|урпа}}, {{cog|mn|арвай}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɑɾ.pɑ/|lang=tr}}
* {{hyphenation|ar|pa|lang=tr}}

===Noun===
{{tr-noun|yı|lar}}

# [[barley]]

====Declension====
{{tr-infl-noun-v|a|poss=1}}

